  "id": "Compound::DB00695 - Gene::759",
  "verbalization": "Furosemide, a loop diuretic, is implicated in the reversible hydration of carbon dioxide through interactions with calcium ions (Ca1). The evidence suggests that Furosemide binds to multiple calcium species, including Ca4, Ca7, and Ca14, all of which participate in the same biochemical pathway. This indicates a potential role for calcium in the metabolic processes affected by Furosemide. The shared participation of these calcium entities in the reversible hydration of carbon dioxide implies a functional link between Furosemide and calcium, possibly through a common pathway or mechanism. The integration of these interactions highlights the importance of calcium in the drug's action, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
